WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.552
Solid. Liquid. Gas.

2
00:00:02.653 --> 00:00:04.984
And four states most people never meet.

3
00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:16.565
Every state of matter is the same atoms, moving at different speeds. Temperature is the dial. Let's turn it.

4
00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:23.659
In a solid, atoms are locked into a lattice. They can't move around, they can only jiggle in place.

5
00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:29.535
Add heat, and the jiggling grows, until the lattice shakes itself apart. That's melting.

6
00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:38.081
Not every atom moves at the same speed. This chart shows the spread: a few slow, a few very fast, most in between.

7
00:00:38.682 --> 00:00:44.478
Follow just one atom, and it never rests. It bumps, slides and wanders through the crowd.

8
00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:53.919
Keep heating, and atoms break free completely. That's boiling. Now they fly in straight lines, and every hit on the piston is pressure.

9
00:00:54.718 --> 00:01:00.481
Push the piston down, and the gas is squeezed back into a liquid, without cooling it at all.

10
00:01:01.481 --> 00:01:09.763
This map shows every state at once. Climb past the critical point, and liquid and gas merge into one: a supercritical fluid.

11
00:01:10.763 --> 00:01:19.689
Now, cold and at very low pressure, ice skips the liquid entirely and turns straight into vapour. That's sublimation, like dry ice.

12
00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:28.450
Heat a liquid from below, and warm atoms rise while cooler ones sink. That loop is convection, the engine of weather.

13
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:37.731
At thousands of degrees, electrons are ripped off their atoms. That's plasma: the stuff of stars, lightning and neon signs.

14
00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:48.619
Go the other way, to billionths of a degree above absolute zero, and atoms merge into one quantum super-atom: a Bose–Einstein condensate.

15
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:57.501
And if you pump every atom out? Even empty space isn't empty. Pairs of particles flicker into existence, and vanish.

16
00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.137
Temperature is just atoms moving.

17
00:02:03.237 --> 00:02:04.980
Pressure can change states too.

18
00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:06.812
And there are more states than three.

19
00:02:08.433 --> 00:02:10.775
Next time: elements and bonds.
